DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ddeevviiccee__ggeett__iivvaarrss() function returns the bus-specific instance vari‐
     ables of a device.

     The ddeevviiccee__sseett__iivvaarrss() function sets the bus-specific instance variables
     of a device.

     Typically, only bus drivers will use these functions.  The kernel assumes
     that the bus driver will manage this memory, and no automatic memory al‐
     location or deallocation happens.  Client drivers should access ivars
     through the BUS_READ_IVAR(9) interface instead.

